;;-*-Lisp-*-
;; Dreamcast target configuration: original console memory sizes (AI-assisted).
;; gcommon enables BIG_MEMORY, which (through PC_BIG_MEMORY) triples the shared
;; process heap behind every dead pool (PROCESS_HEAP_MULT 3, about 2.9 MiB) and
;; every buffer scaled by it (display's DMA buffers, engine matrices, draw counts).
;; The Dreamcast has 16 MiB of RAM in total, so this explicit context, preloaded
;; after gcommon and before gkernel-h, restores the original multiplier of 1.
;; No original body is changed. PC_PORT stays enabled. See TARGET_CONFIG_AUDIT.md.
;;
;; defglobalconstant binds the GOOS value UNEVALUATED, so PC_BIG_MEMORY must be
;; the literal #f: binding the form (and PC_PORT BIG_MEMORY) would leave a
;; non-empty list, which #if treats as true. (Corrected 2026-10-27: the earlier
;; form kept the 3x multiplier; see MEMORY_BUDGET.md.)
(defglobalconstant BIG_MEMORY #f)
(defglobalconstant PC_BIG_MEMORY #f)
